campaignTrail_temp.questions_json = JSON.parse("[{\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 714, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 1, \"description\": \"(SEP. 1986) Mr. Iacocca, a 'Draft I' campaign has caught your staff's attention. Apparently, a group of political consultants, beltway insiders, and a few citizen groups have been building an organization to draft you as a candidate for the Democratic Presidential nomination. Do you think we should respond to this?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 715, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 1, \"description\": \"(JUNE 1987) The Draft I campaign, launched a year ago, urged you to seek the Democratic nomination for President. After some initial reluctance, you entered the race on the strength of promising poll numbers. You’ve assembled a campaign team made up of figures from both Draft I and Washington, D.C., led chiefly by your young campaign manager, Joe Trippi. You’ve chosen to announce your candidacy at The Fist in Detroit. What themes would you like to strike in your speech?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 716, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 1, \"description\": \"(AUGUST 1987) It’s been about two months since you launched your presidential bid, and you’re holding steady at around 10% in the polls. Your opponents are attacking, calling you an out-of-touch millionaire and inexperienced. At the Iowa State Fair’s televised debate with Governor Dukakis, Rep. Gephardt, Senator Gore, and others, the moderator, Russ Van Dyke, asks you about the ''character issue'' - a nod to your divorce and lack of a ''presidential'' image in the wake of the Gary Hart scandal. How will you respond?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 717, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 2, \"description\": \"(JAN 1988) The Iowa caucus is fast approaching, and with each passing day, the complexities of the caucus system and the unpredictable weather of the Hawkeye State dominate conversations among the D.C. press corps. Polls have consistently placed you in second, trailing Gephardt by a narrow margin. How would you like to approach this situation, sir?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 718, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 2, \"description\": \"(MAY 1988) It's the night of the May 3rd primaries. You’re watching TV in your suite at the Omni Netherland Plaza in Cincinnati as the results pour in. You've won Indiana and Ohio decisively, though Washington D.C. slipped away, as expected. Your last serious opponents, Dick Gephardt and Michael Dukakis, were hoping for a weaker showing to push for a contested convention. But tonight, you're the clear winner. The press is waiting downstairs, and it’s obvious this is the turning point for your campaign. What do you do?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 7178, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 2, \"description\": \"(JULY 1988) With your nomination secured, and the Democratic National Convention on the horizon, you need to select a running mate for Vice President. Names ranging from Congressman Gephardt, Senator Bentsen, and Reverend Jackson have been suggested - and given your uneasy relationship with the party this is a more serious decision than per-usual. What do you think?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 734, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 2, \"description\": \"You have just been nominated for President at the DNC in the distractingly large Superdome in New Orleans, Louisiana, shortly after BLANK BLANK was nominated for Vice President. Sitting backstage, sipping coffee and chatting with Joe Trippi, the topic turns to the inevitable: your speech. Your team has been working on a few drafts, but the decision is with you, sir.\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 7299, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"Since your rise in national politics, several moderate Democrats and liberals have expressed dissatisfaction with your candidacy and rhetoric. This has led to the 'Never-Iacocca' faction within the party and prompted former Republican Congressman Pete McCloskey to launch an independent bid with Joseph Duffey, former Chair of the National Endowment for the Humanities, as his running mate. McCloskey is positioning himself as a sensible, liberal alternative to you. How should we respond? \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 732, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"Now that the nomination drama is behind us, it’s time to focus on the general election. George Bush has secured the GOP nomination, defeating Bob Dole and others, and was officially nominated at the RNC in St. Louis, MO. How do you see us taking the fight to Vice President Bush? \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 756, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"With both you and Bush officially nominated by your respective parties, the general election is now underway. At this point, would you like to shift or change any of your messaging, and approach? \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 7199, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"CYOA QUESTION ABOUT RUNNING MATE. COMPLEX DEEP CYOA. not really… \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 7189, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"Sir, at the moment, you are not running any ads. During the primaries, you ran some regional ads, albeit sporadically. Meanwhile, in the last week, Vice President Bush’s campaign has launched a full-scale, negative ad blitz, focusing on your controversial remarks and critiques from your primary opponents. How should we respond to this? \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 719, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 3, \"description\": \"Despite the slightly more uneasy nature of this election cycle, particularly surrounding your candidacy, the Presidential debates remain a tried-and-true tradition. What's your strategy for the upcoming first televised debate?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 725, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"The Bush campaign is attacking your opposition to the invasion of Grenada and the bombing of Libya, insinuating you are a dove. What is your response?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 745, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Given Japan's growing dominance in foreign trade and increasing economic woes at home, do you believe implementing protectionist measures is necessary to safeguard American industries and economic interests?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 754, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Could more have been done to prevent the current farm crisis, which has devastated the upper Midwest?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 724, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"The Bush campaign is criticizing your record regarding your opposition to the MX Missiles proposal and your (failed) amendment to the bill, which would've cut funding for the missiles back in 1981, as well as your broader opposition to the defense/foreign policy of the Reagan administration. Would you like to respond to this?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 726, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"The Bush campaign has repeatedly called you a \\u201cliberal\\u201d or \\u201cthe liberal Senator\\u201d, and so on, as well as pressing your relationship with McGovern and your work as his campaign manager back in 1972 as evidence of your so called \\u201cleft-wing agenda\\u201d. Do you wish to respond to this?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 728, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Television advertising is coming to dominate the political campaign season. Back in 1984, the Reagan campaign used it for primarily positive ads; the Bush campaign does not share that same view and is running a plethora of ads, many of which are negative. Where should we focus your campaign's ads?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 928, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Coming up you have a few days open on your campaign schedule, what would you like to do with this time?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 727, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Some Democrats, since your 1984 campaign, have viewed you with distrust and some with dislike. Some cite your comments regarding Carter and Mondale as weak and inept, while others cite the attacks levied by the Mondale and Dukakis campaigns on your views on the issues of organized labor and trade. How do you want to approach this?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 735, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"It’s time for the Vice Presidential Debate! What themes would you like your running mate, John Glenn, to focus on on the debate stage against Dan Quayle?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 723, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Do you believe that there should be federal funding for abortions?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 753, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"What measures should be taken to assist states, such as Texas, which have been hurt by the recent crash in oil prices?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 749, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Do you support additional gun control measures at the federal level?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 722, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"How will you address the Iran-Contra scandal as you campaign for President?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 733, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 5, \"description\": \"It’s happening again!? In recent days, a claim by an investigative reporter is threatening to destroy your campaign! The reporter claims that before the convention, about 3-4 months ago, you followed a woman into her home, were photographed there, and left sometime the following morning. Though the photos do exist, they aren’t quite irrefutable, but regardless many believe the rumors. \", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 721, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Since the primaries you have made a big deal out of education reform, and ‘redirecting the national focus’ towards education, in particular STEM fields. How exactly do envision addressing these issues?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 743, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"Are you willing to rule out any further increases to the federal income tax, if elected President?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 742, \"fields\": {\"priority\": 4, \"description\": \"What is your position on capital punishment?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.question\", \"pk\": 755, \"fields\": {\"priority\": -1, \"description\": \"Where would you like to spend your final few days on the campaign trail?\", \"likelihood\": 1.0}}]");
campaignTrail_temp.answers_json = JSON.parse("[{\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4484, \"fields\": {\"question\": 743, \"description\": \"Let's have an honest conversation. My opponent and I both recognize the reality of the economy in this country today, and our deficit and debt issues. While he may not openly admit it, the reality is that taxes very well may have to be raised.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4428, \"fields\": {\"question\": 722, \"description\": \"We will hammer on this theme, and particularly Mr. Bush's claim that he knew nothing about it. The Tower Commission only scratched the surface. This a serious issue, what Oliver North has done was to use the political action committee system to do what they did in Watergate -- launder money.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4413, \"fields\": {\"question\": 716, \"description\": \"I’ve faced challenges most people can’t imagine, getting fired from Ford, turning Chrysler around. I never said I was a perfect person, or pretended to be something that I’m not. I’m not here to be some perfect politician, I’m here to fix real problems. Americans want a leader who takes on tough challenges and wins, and I do. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 6614, \"fields\": {\"question\": 714, \"description\": \"Well, that's flattering, but let's not rush into anything. We need to see if this has serious momentum. Keep an eye on it, gather more information, and we'll discuss it once we have a clearer picture. I want to make sure we're making the right move before diving in.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 6615, \"fields\": {\"question\": 714, \"description\": \"I saw the New York Times wrote something about this damned 'draft'? Let's get a statement out there, making it clear: I have absolutely no intention of running for the Presidency. I'm committed to staying at Chrysler until I'm 65, that's October of '89. We've got work to do here, and I'm not about to jump ship.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9914, \"fields\": {\"question\": 715, \"description\": \"Today, I'm announcing my candidacy for President because it's time to bring American jobs back and fight hard for our nation’s working families. We're going to demand fair trade, stop Washington's inaction, and make our country strong again. Together, we can rebuild America and make it thrive like never before.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9915, \"fields\": {\"question\": 715, \"description\": \"Standing here today, I feel a deep sense of purpose. America stands at a crossroads, and we need strong, decisive leadership to move forward. The political elite have let us down. It's time for real change. Together, we'll challenge special interests, revive American jobs, and make America great again!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9916, \"fields\": {\"question\": 715, \"description\": \"Ladies and gentlemen, our nation is in crisis. Americans are burdened with exorbitant medical bills while politicians in Washington look the other way. When I am President, we will confront the powerful insurance giants, ensuring healthcare is within reach for every citizen, and placing people's needs above corporate gains.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 54414, \"fields\": {\"question\": 716, \"description\": \"This is a ridiculous question. Look, I’m sure the other Democrats on stage have had issues in their personal lives, just like me. I’m sure you have too, Russ. But here’s the difference: I’m straight with people. I tell the truth, even when it’s tough to hear.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4414, \"fields\": {\"question\": 716, \"description\": \"Russ, let’s cut the bullshit. This whole character issue nonsense is a joke. My divorce? My personal life? Spare me. I’ve taken on real, actual challenges, the kind these guys wouldn’t know the first thing about, and I came out on top every damn time.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44417, \"fields\": {\"question\": 71888, \"description\": \"You know, I’ve been called a lot of things in my career, ‘'inexperienced' isn’t one of them. I built my success from the ground up, and I know what it takes to overcome challenges and win. The folks in Washington? They’ve been doing the same thing for years, and it’s not working. It’s time we tried something different.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44416, \"fields\": {\"question\": 71888, \"description\": \"Career politicians have had their shot, and look where it's gotten us! Americans are fed up with the same tired excuses. If you want someone with ‘political experience,’ fine, go vote for someone else. But if you want someone who’s built something, created jobs, and fought for workers, I’m your guy.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44415, \"fields\": {\"question\": 71888, \"description\": \"Look, let’s be honest. Washington’s full of so-called ‘experts,’ and they’ve been at it for years. What’s the result? A mountain of debt, factories shutting down, and jobs heading overseas. My whole career has been about fixing what’s broken, getting people back to work, and I’ll do the same in the White House.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 444415, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7178, \"description\": \"Look, we've been ahead of the Republicans, whether it's Bush or Dole, for what feels like a lifetime. It's time we make a real move, for America. I want to give Jesse Jackson a call.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 644415, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7178, \"description\": \"They’ll never stop with that damned experience question. Fine, we'll pacify the bastards. I want to give Senator Bentsen a call, nobody can argue with the man's record, and maybe he'll convince some Southerners to vote Blue.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 544415, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7178, \"description\": \"Gephardt has been auditioning for the spot since he dropped out. You know, it might be a little on the nose, but I want to sit down with the kid... Looks like he's the best pick.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4415, \"fields\": {\"question\": 718, \"description\": \"Alright, let’s head down there. No point in keeping them waiting.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 441515, \"fields\": {\"question\": 718, \"description\": \"We have a country that is literally on fire, in so many way, and we’re supposed to waste time playing nice? Are you kidding me? We had this nomination locked up months ago, if you ask me.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 3315, \"fields\": {\"question\": 717, \"description\": \"I don’t think we need to be on the ground too much. Let’s buy a buncha airtime across Iowa and barnstorm them with ads. Gephardt’s still got a lead, but hitting them hard with ads could really do the trick.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 33177, \"fields\": {\"question\": 717, \"description\": \"You know it, I know it, the early contests are just media hype. I’m focusing on the Super Tuesday states that Joe keeps talking about. My plan? Three days in Texas, then skip around through the rest of the South.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 3317, \"fields\": {\"question\": 717, \"description\": \"We have what? 12 days till the caucuses? Let’s get on a bus and hit as many fucking counties as we can. Town halls, barbecues, whatever people want. I don’t care if it’s a barn or a backyard - we’re showing up, and shaking hands. That's how you win.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 3316, \"fields\": {\"question\": 717, \"description\": \"I don’t give a damn about Iowa, to be frank. My best numbers are in New Hampshire and the other states that actually matter. Let Gephardt and those other bastards waste their time fighting over that miserable state. They can have it.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4416, \"fields\": {\"question\": 718, \"description\": \"Let's go down there and tell it like it is about my so-called rivals. Gephardt, Dukakis, they're just part of the same old, tired system. They tried to stop us, but look at tonight. We've shown who the real winner is, and it sure isn't them.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4417, \"fields\": {\"question\": 718, \"description\": \"This is the moment we've been working for. Let's show them what real leadership looks like. No more division, no more excuses. It's time to bring this country together and get things done.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 2217, \"fields\": {\"question\": 717777778, \"description\": \"All these candidates, and the press, have failed to see that the West is where the delegates are! I want to spend cash on California, the Mountain States, and the Great Plains.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4418, \"fields\": {\"question\": 719, \"description\": \"When I'm president, one of my eyes will always be on the economy, and I'll make that clear at the debate. I'll protect this country from bad, rigged trade deals and make sure American jobs are secure. That's the job of a president, not giving fancy speeches or stirring up division.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 114418, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7189, \"description\": \"Bush wants to play games? Fine. I’ll run ads exposing his dishonesty on Iran-Contra and how out of touch he is with the real workings of government. I want everyone, even people sitting on their couch, to know this man can't be trusted! \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 114420, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7189, \"description\": \"I don't have time for this nonsense. That's why I have Joe Trippi on board. Let him handle the ads. My job is to hold rallies, meet people, and get actual things done. That's how we're going to win this thing. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 114421, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7189, \"description\": \"We just don’t have the budget for a big ad campaign, and I’m not going to write a check for it. We’ll stick with the rallies, at least for now. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 114419, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7189, \"description\": \"These ads are too expensive. We can afford to buy airtime in the Midwest, and maybe California, but the real strength of this campaign comes from rallies and interviews. That's where we win. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4419, \"fields\": {\"question\": 719, \"description\": \"My strategy is simple: George Bush is not just incompetent, he's downright contemptible. In the debate, I'm going straight at him on trade, he’s helped devastate the Midwest. And don’t forget Iran-Contra, where he lied to the American people. This man is bad news, folks.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 7725, \"fields\": {\"question\": 733, \"description\": \"It's claimed that this 'incident' occurred several months ago, but why is it only being revealed now? This is the most blatant example of voter interference I have ever seen in my life in public service. I'm determined to fight back fiercely and reject bogus accusations by a vast right-wing plot against my innovative ideas and progressive campaign.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 7726, \"fields\": {\"question\": 733, \"description\": \"You know, I want to approach this delicately. I want to appear on 60 Minutes with my wife, Lee. I wish to deny the allegations; the woman I was photographed with was a part of the campaign and a good personal friend of both me and my wife. From there, we will appeal to the American people that I am a family man, and my wife and I have overcome difficulties in our personal lives, but the media should focus on the pressing issues at hand today foremost.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 7727, \"fields\": {\"question\": 733, \"description\": \"I will not even dignify this ridiculous bullshit found in a supermarket tabloid. Let my campaign release a statement denying the allegations and a vague overture towards legal action.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4420, \"fields\": {\"question\": 719, \"description\": \"I want to approach this debate like any candidate should. My goal is simple: to connect with everyday voters. I’m not here to talk down to anyone. I’m here, like Truman or Kennedy, to show that I’m a Democrat who focuses on getting things done for this country.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4421, \"fields\": {\"question\": 719, \"description\": \"Frankly, this campaign is exactly where I want it to be. Debates give the political elites a chance to steer the narrative. Well, not on my watch. As the Democratic nominee, I’ve decided not to participate in any rigged debate.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4422, \"fields\": {\"question\": 720, \"description\": \"no.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4423, \"fields\": {\"question\": 720, \"description\": \"No.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4424, \"fields\": {\"question\": 720, \"description\": \"NO.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4425, \"fields\": {\"question\": 721, \"description\": \"You know, I’ve said this for a long time: I firmly believe that education is the great equalizer in our society. Today we have underserved communities who’s schools desperately need funding, and aid, but a President, and an administration that turns a blind eye.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4426, \"fields\": {\"question\": 721, \"description\": \"You know it isn’t just as simple as education. It comes down to: bolstering job training, revitalizing teaching methods, and creating new fields altogether. Our commitment goes beyond the classroom; it's about empowering families, students and workers. We need an approach that embraces innovation and offers a range of opportunities tailored to different needs.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4427, \"fields\": {\"question\": 721, \"description\": \"Education is <em>really</em> the key to America's competitive dominance in the 21st century, yet, instead of preparing our children for the world of the future, we are letting them fall further behind. During my administration that will change, we will modernize schools, increase student loan programs, and, expand programs for mathematics, foreign language, and computer studies.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9999, \"fields\": {\"question\": 928, \"description\": \"We need to shore up labor and Midwestern support; let's visit the Tioga Marine in Philadelphia, PA. We'll address blue-collar workers, highlighting how George Bush's economic policies favor the wealthy and big corporations. Furthermore, we must emphasize that economic growth can only happen if our steel and automobile industries are strong.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9998, \"fields\": {\"question\": 928, \"description\": \"I want to visit the Black majority, Lyons Unity Baptist Church in Houston, TX, and speak about the lack of economic leadership today and that, increasingly, the very people who are working the hardest are the very poorest. We must assure those who are following the rules and working 40 hours a week that we will raise them out of poverty and make this country fairer.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 9997, \"fields\": {\"question\": 928, \"description\": \"Let's start with Billings, Montana, and take a detour to the Mountain and Plain States. I want to speak to the fact that our campaign has a simple message: economic restructuring through investment and rebuilding the foundation of this nation's economy: our farms, our natural resources, our factories, and most of all, our educational system, so that it's the best in the world.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4429, \"fields\": {\"question\": 722, \"description\": \"I want the American people to take a look at my record. For over a decade I have worked to fight for the underdog, and what I believe is right for the future generations of this country. I have worked for, and been supported by millions of Coloradians who I am happy to call friends. Can George Bush say the same?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4430, \"fields\": {\"question\": 722, \"description\": \"Isn’t attacking Bush on Iran-Contra like ‘beating a dead horse’ at this point? It’s an overly partisan issue, and frankly I don’t think there’s not much to gain coming out too aggressively.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4431, \"fields\": {\"question\": 723, \"description\": \"I support any federal effort to increase the health and well-being of women in America.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4432, \"fields\": {\"question\": 723, \"description\": \"I have an open mind on this issue, but it would depend on who needs the money and what case they can make during the federal budget process.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4433, \"fields\": {\"question\": 723, \"description\": \"This is definitely taking things too far. The <em>Roe v. Wade</em> case is settled law, but federal funding for the practice is an entirely different matter.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4434, \"fields\": {\"question\": 724, \"description\": \"During my time in the Senate, I actively opposed the proposal of MX Missles, and I had one of the most anti-Reagan voting records in Congress. Because I have always believed the way to keep us safe is not through bloated budgets but through reform and sustained innovation.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4435, \"fields\": {\"question\": 724, \"description\": \"It's best if we don't address this head-on. We can attack the general foreign policy of Reagan/Bush, but going into specifics like this will only make the attacks more biting. Let's instead focus on the scandals like Iran-Contra and The Vice Presidents' murky role in it or the struggles faced by our farmers in the current crisis.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4436, \"fields\": {\"question\": 724, \"description\": \"The people of America need to resist these attempts by the Bush campaign to smear my record and my positions. Let me make it clear that I only opposed certain aspects of the bill. My unwavering commitment is, of course, to ensure our safety and incorporate new technology into our military.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4437, \"fields\": {\"question\": 725, \"description\": \"We must counterattack Reagan and Bush for the pointless increases in defense spending, which have destroyed the federal budget this decade. As we approach the 21st century, we need a lean armed force that relies primarily on intelligence and diplomacy and serves against the realities of warfare and terrorism in the coming century.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4438, \"fields\": {\"question\": 725, \"description\": \"Since I heard John Kennedy speaking about global threats and worldwide suffering as a young man, I have known that America needs to actively defend the downtrodden worldwide, where appropriate. As far as military action, it should be taken only in protection of our security interests, when clear and achievable objectives are laid out, and when exhaustion of nonmilitary options occurs.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4439, \"fields\": {\"question\": 725, \"description\": \"While we can discuss certain aspects, I believe the actions in Grenada and Libya were necessary to counter communist threats. We must remain vigilant in defending democracy and supporting our allies in the fight against terrorism and aggression.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4440, \"fields\": {\"question\": 726, \"description\": \"I take pride in standing on the opposite side of the political idelogy espoused by Ronald Reagan and George Bush. Rather than advocating for extreme defense spending without addressing the needs of farmers and laborers, I am dedicated to representing all Americans and continuing the legacy of outstanding leaders like Harry Truman and Jack Kennedy.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4441, \"fields\": {\"question\": 726, \"description\": \"The Bush campaign continues to use dishonest language to scare the American people. Going back to my race in 1984, and before that in the Senate, I have proudly represented a fresh perspective within the Democratic Party, advocating for progressive reform and practical solutions to the challenges that the 21st century will bring.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4442, \"fields\": {\"question\": 726, \"description\": \"It doesn't matter what the \\u201clabel\\u201d is that we use. The important thing is the issues we will decide upon.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4443, \"fields\": {\"question\": 727, \"description\": \"Look, during campaigns our party expresses its views. It sometimes gets a little messy, but that’s the nature of our process, and democracy itself. I am the nominee, but the Democratic Party has a broad scope, wide membership, but the same goals.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4444, \"fields\": {\"question\": 727, \"description\": \"I don’t think it’s prudent that we respond directly, but there’s no harm in bringing in some more populist themes in our campaign speech, like my plan to revitalize our infrastructure, and my plans for trade deals with emerging markets, where our products can flood!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4445, \"fields\": {\"question\": 727, \"description\": \"You know, frankly, the primary is over, and it's time for us to look ahead. I'm focused on beating George Bush and delivering real change for the American people, not getting bogged down in an inter-party debate.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4446, \"fields\": {\"question\": 728, \"description\": \"Let's talk about my personal story, beginning with my childhood in Ottawa, Kansas, and leading up to my career as an attorney for the Justice Department, director of the McGovern campaign, and ultimately my tenure in the Senate. My guiding principle has always been to stand up for the underdog.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4447, \"fields\": {\"question\": 728, \"description\": \"Let's run aggressive attack ads against George Bush. We can target him as a creature of his political handlers who lacks any deep-seated convictions or passion. Let's also throw in some spots attacking his profound lack of leadership, and action during the scandals of the Reagan years.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4448, \"fields\": {\"question\": 728, \"description\": \"Look, there's a lot of polling saying Americans are anxious about Reaganomics and the stability of our economy. I want to run ads about the deficit, average wages, and the 'voodoo' economics of the Reagan years, and compare it to my common sense beliefs on the economy. Let's also mix in some spots to defend against Bush's dishonest allegations on various issues.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4449, \"fields\": {\"question\": 729, \"description\": \"You know, I'd be shocked if Anderson even cracks 2% in the polls. This guy's a loser, frankly. We’re not wasting time on him. Our focus is on winning the damn White House, and that's exactly what we're gonna do.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 444949, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7291, \"description\": \"Well, Jesus fucking Christ, I’ll be damned. These do-nothing, technocratic Democrats are a fucking stain on the party and, frankly, on the country. I’m not wasting another word on Tsongas or the rest of that sorry bunch.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 445151, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7291, \"description\": \"I didn’t think it would come to this, honestly. Looks like Tsongas is hell-bent on making this fucking race an even bigger mess. Well... better late than never, I guess. Let’s start toning down the rhetoric. That’s all we can do now. They want a leader, and I can give them that.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44491, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7299, \"description\": \"Who? Look, this guy is just a tiny little thorn in our side, and I don’t think we should alter our message at all. Those bastards, well, they’ll just end up voting for Bush anyway. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4451, \"fields\": {\"question\": 729, \"description\": \"Look, I’m telling you, this race is gonna be decided at the margins, and Anderson could really mess things up for us. We can’t afford to ignore that. It wouldn’t kill us to dial down the rhetoric a notch and show them the 'Presidential' Iacocca the media’s been itching to see. They want a leader, and I can give them that.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44511, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7299, \"description\": \"Look, I’m telling you, this race is gonna be decided at the margins, and McCloskey could really mess things up for us. We can’t afford to ignore that. It wouldn’t kill us to dial down the rhetoric a notch and show them the 'Presidential' Iacocca the media’s been itching to see. They want a leader, and I can give them that.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4452, \"fields\": {\"question\": 730, \"description\": \"I will mention this aspect of my biography frequently, particularly in contrast with Dan Quayle.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4453, \"fields\": {\"question\": 730, \"description\": \"It wouldn't hurt to mix in some old photographs of myself in Navy dress with the tough-on-defense ads we run.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4454, \"fields\": {\"question\": 730, \"description\": \"I served honorably in the U.S.Navy, but Bush was basically a war hero. We should focus on areas where we have more of an advantage.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4458, \"fields\": {\"question\": 732, \"description\": \"We’ve got to make America great again, and that starts with raising the living standards for everyone, not just the privileged few. For the last 8 years, we’ve had a government that’s ignored the working class and the less-privileged. As President, I’ll make sure every American has the pride of a job and a real stake in our economy.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4459, \"fields\": {\"question\": 732, \"description\": \"You know, at every rally, we need to make it clear just how much of a liar George Bush is. Whether he's twisting my business record, putting down the lowest amongst us, or brushing off Iran-Contra, he’s trouble. We can’t afford to let this guy win, and we won’t. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4159, \"fields\": {\"question\": 732, \"description\": \"Bush is part of the old guard, the same folks who’ve been in Washington for years, not fixing a damn thing. Factories are closing, people are out of work, and all he’s done is talk. Talk doesn’t fix problems. We need real solutions. I’m not a politician, I’m a businessman. I’ve turned companies around, and I’ll turn this country around.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44463, \"fields\": {\"question\": 734, \"description\": \"You know what? It’s time to take the fight straight to George Bush and the Republicans. We’ll call out their failures, point by point, and show people why we’re the only real choice for genuine, progressive change.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 444634, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7344, \"description\": \"This is just noise from the press. Jesse’s a likable, and good guy, who happens to be a fighter. I stand by my choice, no question whatsoever.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 444633, \"fields\": {\"question\": 7344, \"description\": \"Listen, I know some people, especially white folks, might not like Jesse. But let me tell you, he’s the future of politics in this country. I want him by my side at those rallies. He’s my partner in this fight, and that’s not up for debate.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4444633, \"fields\": {\"question\": 73444, \"description\": \"Listen, I like Dick. He's a good-hearted, hard-working family man. In politics, finding someone who not only sees eye-to-eye with you on the big stuff but also has real character? That’s rare. And I trust him to fire up the base and bring folks together when it counts on the campaign trail.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 44446633, \"fields\": {\"question\": 734444, \"description\": \"Senator Bentsen is the best Washington has to offer, and he’s a fine man. Ask anyone, Democrat or Republican, and they'll tell you about his decency and courage. He's got character, and I can't think of anyone better prepared to be Vice President, or, God willing, President of this great nation.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 54463, \"fields\": {\"question\": 734, \"description\": \"Honestly, Joe, the stakes are way too high to be winging it. Let’s take the best parts of these drafts and tighten them up. I want this speech to be sharp and snappy, no fluff. We need to leave no doubt, especially with the damned press.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4463, \"fields\": {\"question\": 734, \"description\": \"These speeches are too damn sanitized. People don’t want rehearsed lines; they want the truth. I’m tossing these drafts out. I’ll speak directly about what matters, bringing back jobs, standing up to unfair trade, and making America strong again.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4464, \"fields\": {\"question\": 734, \"description\": \"Look, Joe, I've never been one for fancy words or political jargon. Let's keep it simple. I'll thank everyone and get straight to the point. It's time for real leadership and real solutions.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4465, \"fields\": {\"question\": 735, \"description\": \"Let’s really challenge the all-or-nothing approach of Reaganomics head-on. Senator Glenn should focus on his ability to address uncertainty and mismanagement in government and the economy by working in a bipartisan, transparent, and reform-minded manner. Additionally let’s focus on the fact that Senator Quayle's record on defense matters and the future transformation of our industries for the 21st century is practically non-existent.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 3365, \"fields\": {\"question\": 735, \"description\": \"I want Senator Glenn to focus on the obvious: Dan Quayle is undeniably unfit to be President of the United States, and the fact that despite Quayle's lack of experience and expertise, says a lot about the decision making on the top of the ticket. The Senator can also talk about his record of simply, improving the lives and economic status of his constituents.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4478, \"fields\": {\"question\": 742, \"description\": \"You know, I understand this deeply important issue is complex, and often divisive. But while valuing human life, I recognize the necessity of responding to the most heinous crimes threatening our communities, and I do support capital punishment.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4479, \"fields\": {\"question\": 742, \"description\": \"I believe, if a state wishes to impose capital punishment, that it should have every right to do so. Frankly, people at a local level can come to reasonable solutions and consensus on this important issue better than the Federal government.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4480, \"fields\": {\"question\": 742, \"description\": \"I have held this belief since before my career in public service; capital punishment is fundamentally an ineffective deterrent at reducing crime, and is not applied in an equal or fair manner. I do not, and will not, support the practice.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4481, \"fields\": {\"question\": 743, \"description\": \"As President, you can count on me to roll up my sleeves and give it my all when it comes to cutting income taxes for middle-class, and working Americans. I'm all about putting money back where it belongs – in your wallets, and making sure our tax system's fair.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4483, \"fields\": {\"question\": 743, \"description\": \"I genuinely hope that we won't find ourselves in such a situation, and as it stands now, I wouldn’t, but it would be silly to dismiss any possibility at this juncture. Our commitment to responsible, and honest leadership demands nothing less.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4489, \"fields\": {\"question\": 745, \"description\": \"There are better solutions than resorting to protectionist measures. Instead, my focus is on innovative education, especially STEM, and initiating a process of industrial modernization. That blueprint will lead America into the 21st century as the greatest global power with a dynamic, competitive, open economy.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4490, \"fields\": {\"question\": 745, \"description\": \"First, I would meet with Japanese leaders and all foreign leaders and representatives with a framework of striving for free-but-fair trade. We must and will focus on cooperation and mutual innovation, but I wouldn't take anything off the table.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4491, \"fields\": {\"question\": 745, \"description\": \"During these challenging times, we must address the impact of unchecked trade on American workers and industries. We must prioritize our nation's interests and take a resolute stance on safeguarding our economy and jobs. As President, I would run an Administration that puts American workers first and ensures a fair playing field in global trade.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4501, \"fields\": {\"question\": 749, \"description\": \"This is getting it completely backwards. American families have every right to defend themselves from the wave of violent crime we see across this country.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4502, \"fields\": {\"question\": 749, \"description\": \"I believe it's crucial to find common-sense solutions to address this. First of all, I would support limited steps on this issue, like a ban on “cop killer” bullets. Overall, though, I would be reluctant to take big steps either way on the issue without national consensus.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4503, \"fields\": {\"question\": 749, \"description\": \"We have a national crime epidemic today, and I’ve long supported stronger Federal legislation regulating the importing and interstate sales of firearms, a required waiting period and mandatory added sentences for people who use a firearm while committing a Federal crime.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4511, \"fields\": {\"question\": 753, \"description\": \"We must forge an energy strategy that revitalizes our commitment to domestic oil production. Reinstating price support is essential, as it not only bolsters our energy independence but also safeguards the livelihoods of hardworking Americans in the industry. By embracing forward-thinking policies, we can ensure that our nation remains a pioneer in energy innovation while providing vital support to the communities that fuel our progress.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4512, \"fields\": {\"question\": 753, \"description\": \"I firmly believe that American companies, working in collaboration with our trusted allies, should have the right to bid on foreign oil contracts, thereby fostering international cooperation and ensuring our energy security.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4513, \"fields\": {\"question\": 753, \"description\": \"Cheap oil is an overall benefit to our economy. I think the majority of voters will understand that this fall.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4514, \"fields\": {\"question\": 753, \"description\": \"I think everyone can see we need more substantial funding for federal programs to effectively mitigate the worst effects of this downturn. Today, regrettably, we have a federal government that too often fails to harness its power to aid the average citizen, and that is fundamentally wrong.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4515, \"fields\": {\"question\": 754, \"description\": \"Unfortunately, as the economy changes and we move into the 21st century, we must realize there are too many farmers in this country. We invest in vocational training and education to move these displaced workers into thriving new industries.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4516, \"fields\": {\"question\": 754, \"description\": \"The best way to deal with this is not protectionism. It is, instead, modernizing and empowering our farmers to thrive in the global market. I envision an America that engages in innovative trade agreements with countries like the Soviet Union, Mexico, and others, to open up new markets for our agricultural products. By being pragmatic, we can ensure that these deals boost our exports and protect our farmers’ interests, allowing them to be competitive and booming in the 21st century.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4517, \"fields\": {\"question\": 754, \"description\": \"As a proud son of the West, it pains me to see the hardship faced by the farmers who raised me. When I am elected President, I will take bold action to stabilize the situation with assertive federal intervention. My focus would be immediate relief through low-interest loans, debt relief, and targeted assistance. Embracing innovation and sustainable agriculture, coupled with fair trade deals, would pave the way for our farmers' resilience and success on the global stage. Protecting our nation's backbone is paramount, and as President, I'd stand united with those who feed our nation.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4518, \"fields\": {\"question\": 755, \"description\": \"Let’s start by hitting Michigan, and then go campaigning through Wisconsin, Minnesota, and end with visiting South Dakota. It’s not a secret the labor voter isn’t exactly hyper-enthusiastic about our campaign, and we need to make sure our coalition stands.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4519, \"fields\": {\"question\": 755, \"description\": \"I want to start in Houston, Texas, and travel throughout the state, holding rallies with local and state officials. We can also cross over into Louisiana, and hold some last-minute rallies too.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4520, \"fields\": {\"question\": 755, \"description\": \"California, Oregon and Washington are three states that we’ve gotta win. Let’s target all three of them, hitting Los Angeles, San Francisco, then cross over into Portland, and up into Seattle.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4521, \"fields\": {\"question\": 755, \"description\": \"I’ve seen some recent polls showing a tight race in Pennsylvania and Ohio. Let’s barnstorm through Pittsburgh and New Castle, and then cross into Ohio, and campaign through Youngstown, Canton and end in Cleveland. That will push our margins up, surely.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4523, \"fields\": {\"question\": 756, \"description\": \"America’s lost its way, and it’s time to bring back some good old-fashioned common sense. I’ve spent my life tackling tough challenges, fixing what’s broken, and delivering results. George Bush and the Republicans? They have no clue what real Americans are facing. I do.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4524, \"fields\": {\"question\": 756, \"description\": \"We need to center this campaign on my trade message. Plain and simple, our country is getting ripped off, and that’s not right. The Japanese? They’re fine folks, but they, along with many others, are getting rich by outsmarting us, while we foolishly export our industrial base!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4525, \"fields\": {\"question\": 756, \"description\": \"We can tweak it a bit, but the core message stays the same: I make deals. George Bush? Nobody likes him, and he hasn’t gotten a damn thing done. I’ve spent my life in high-pressure business and come out on top. I’ll do the same with the Soviet Union and get business and labor working here at home.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer\", \"pk\": 4526, \"fields\": {\"question\": 756, \"description\": \"I’m not changing a thing. I want to keep hammering home that I’m not a politician, I’m a businessman, and I know how the economy really works. George Bush and the political class? They don’t have a clue.\"}}]");
