campaignTrail_temp.answer_feedback_json = JSON.parse("[{\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1973, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4501, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a mainstream position for a Republican to take...\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1893, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4413, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a honest, good answer. While the question of personal integrity persists, the American people largely like and trust you. Divorce, once a significant concern for a would-be President, seems less impactful as the years roll by.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4159, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a populist line to take against the Vice President, and while it’s true this kind of rhetoric worked well for you in the primaries, it’s unclear how it will land against George Bush.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1894, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 54414, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"It doesn’t take a detective to see the anger in your face or hear it in your voice, it’s not for show. Some of your supporters in the audience snicker at your remark, but you know the press will spin this as a tense, or difficult moment for you.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1894, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4414, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The audience eats up your response, but your assertiveness could be seen as too harsh. While it resonates with voters tired of establishment politics, you should consider adding a touch of humility to balance it out.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1894, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9914, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your speech has garnered quite a bit of press attention. It's already evident that you're positioning yourself as a bold, economic populist. However, the Democratic establishment doesn't seem to be taking your candidacy all that seriously. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1894, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9915, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your speech got a lot of press coverage, but many noted its vague and non-ideological tone. Attacking the political establishment can draw attention and build a base, but you'll need solid policy backbone to sustain your campaign in the long-run.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1894, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9916, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your speech was widely reported and shocked many political pundits. Most people weren’t expecting an announcement rich with policy commitments and clear ideological positioning. For better or worse, you’ve firmly established yourself as a liberal Democrat.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4416, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The press takes countless photos of you, practically milking the media with your smiles, boasts, and occasional hints of sharpness. With Dukakis and Gephardt’s campaigns imploding, your happy face is set to be the top story in tomorrow’s news.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4464, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You ended up sticking very loosely to a prepared script. Your markedly unsteady reading at times, and overly rapid reading at others, was obviously noticed by viewers. The bored reception from your usually ravenous supporters in the Superdome made it clear, even to you, that this speech was a flub. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4502, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is probably the closest you could get to a middle-ground on this heated question, even if conservatives are ideologically opposed to gun control, there is too undeniably serious bouts of crime in major cities.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4463, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your supporters in the Superdome appreciate your long-winded and revolving style. But the political press is less forgiving of your bird walks, and despite some good lines, are openly reporting on your 'unabashed laziness' as a candidate, and speech-giver.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44463, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"From the onset of your speech, it was obvious you'd be taking the attack to the Republican Party and President Bush by extension. Your supporters were eager to hear you on the offensive, but it's still unclear if this strategy will quite work in November.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 444634, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Reverend Jackson’s spot on your ticket is still upsetting white moderates and those with racial concerns. While it’s unclear exactly how much it’s impacted your poll numbers, there’s no doubt it has, to some extent.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4444633, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Congressman Gephardt from Missouri was the clear favorite for your running mate according to the press, and he had the backing of much of your senior campaign staff. While you’re not spending as much time with him on the trail as you might with another running mate, he’s eager to rally the heartland and energize the base. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44446633, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Lloyd Bentsen was a name you kept pushing from the start, even when your staff wasn’t fully on board. The Texas Senator is seen as one of the most moderate, maybe even conservative, Democrats left in Washington, and selecting him as your running mate, is doubling down on some of your moderate stances.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 444633, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Though your choice of Reverend Jackson sparked controversy, your decision to bring him along to rallies and embrace him as an ally is starting to win over your base. Still, many white voters hold long-standing resentment towards Jackson and other perceived 'black radicals.' \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 54463, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You sat down shortly before prime time to make the final changes to your speech with Trippi. Ultimately, on the big stage, you stuck closely to the prepared lines. With some laughs, cheers, and a few boos directed towards the GOP, it seemed to go about as well as could have been expected.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4415, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Once you step out and face the cameras, you give it to them straight, like you always do. You’re here to win, and no one’s going to stop you. Washington’s had its chance, and look where it’s gotten us. It’s time for something new, and you’re the one to make it happen. Your words, firm and direct: 'We’ve proven we can win. And we’re going to keep winning.'\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 441515, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You walk down and quickly start talking a thousand words a minute about how rigged the Democratic Primary has been and how you have ‘'no respect'’ for your remaining rivals. Would it kill you to show a little humility, sir?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44417, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your response draws a small chuckle from the audience. Meanwhile, your rivals on stage, feeling the weight of their polling numbers, appear noticeably more tense and defensive, taking a sharper tone than you tonight.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44416, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The debates are really getting to you, huh? Sure, your supporters love seeing you fired up, but the press doesn’t. Those ‘nasty’ headlines won’t stop until you tone it down.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 544415, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Congressman Gephardt stayed in the race longer than some of your other competitors, but with a serious race for the Presidency under his belt and his identity as a populist set in stone, he, even before he dropped out, was considered the obvious choice for your number two.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 444415, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"It's no secret that your selection of a running mate has higher salience due to the unique circumstances of your rise, and Jesse Jackson will certainly help with press attention. However, many in the nation are left thinking this was a haphazard and seriously flawed pick, especially given your lack of experience and relationship with the party's establishment.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 644415, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Though there is some dismay in your camp regarding the boringness of Lloyd Bentsen, he is a steady, trusted, and able man, and should hopefully calm the nerves of the establishment and conservative Democrats who are anxious about your candidacy.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44415, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your supporters in the audience break out into applause. It’s clear you are sticking to your outsider credentials, and firing back at the political establishment.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1893, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 6615, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The media is eager to report on your statement. Though a Presidential bid from you was never taken too seriously, it has still inspired plenty of press coverage. It's sure to remain a topic in the national press for some time, at least until the primary campaign season properly kicks off...\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1893, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 6613, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your speech and fiery words have started your campaign with a bang, with snippets of your speech playing on television and recounted in the pen of the press during the early months of the primary season. Though there is some concern about alienating moderate voters necessary for the general election, this is a strong tone to set.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1893, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 6614, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Fair enough. Some in the press are already writing op-eds about your potential candidacy. Some are negative, some positive, but most treat your candidacy as a wild card, if not outright a publicity stunt. The 'Draft I' campaign has already been taking polls and releasing them to the press. To your glee, you are performing surprisingly well.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 2217, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Ultimately, you got clobbered on Super Tuesday, winning only Washington, Hawaii, and Wyoming. You fought until the convention valiantly, though with a delegate deficit most of the time, much like in 1984. Except this time, you narrowly won.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 33177, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your numbers down South have always been in doubt given Jackson, and Gore’s lockhold on the region, but your short tour of the Lone Star state, and then hop around the broader South are giving you an incredibly boisterous, and good reception.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 3317, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"After a few days on the road in Iowa, on your 'grand tour', sleeping in hotels, shaking hands, and giving speeches all day, has taken its toll. But Gephardt’s lead is starting to narrow, and the possibility of a victory here feels more real with each passing day.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 3315, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"In spite of your hefty spending in the Hawkeye State, it doesn’t seem to be enough. Gephardt’s lead in Iowa, though small, isn’t budging. Still, second place in your first-ever caucus isn’t so bad, is it?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 3316, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This enrages some on your campaign staff, and Joe Trippi, your campaign manager, even threatens to resign. You agree to some limited visits in Iowa, but with a clear focus on New Hampshire and the other upcoming contests.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1895, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4417, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You step downstairs and deliver your remarks. The press didn’t expect such a calm tone from you, sir. After your statement, you hold a brief press conference, purposely refraining from calling for Gephardt and Dukakis to drop out. Is this the new, more presidential Lee Iacocca?..\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1896, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 114418, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Negative ads are pumped out and soon air nationwide. The Bush campaign is eager and willing to deny the charges and allegations made, but the damage is done, for better or worse.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1896, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 114421, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Stubbornness might have worked in business, but the Bush campaign isn't playing by those rules. Their ads are hitting hard, and the latest polling and favorability ratings show it's hurting you, and your chances at victory. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1896, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 114420, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Trippi, your campaign manager, eagerly takes the reins and oversees the rollout of some ads. They focus on your upbringing and life story, a bit expensive and somewhat off-brand for you. For a brief moment, it feels like you're running a typical campaign. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1896, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 114419, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You run positive ads about your economic platform in the Midwest and California, but the Bush campaign is quickly buying up ad space across the country, and it looks like they are hitting with a very negative tone.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1896, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4418, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"From the start of the Pittsburgh debate, the economy was your focus. You pressed Bush on job losses and stagnant wages, while he questioned your judgment, and so-called erratic character. The debate was widely considered a draw.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1897, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4419, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The first televised debate was held in Cincinnati, Ohio, and right from the start, it was clear things were going to get wild. Bush was visibly angry during points in the debate. Despite this, you kept your focus locked on the Vice President, hitting him hard nearly every time you spoke. In the end, this will galvanize your supporters, and his too.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1898, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 7727, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your half-response didn’t go over well with the media, let alone go over at all, as it was one mere statement. Most Americans believe the allegations against you, and with no response against it besides a written threat, many are growing to view you negatively.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1898, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4420, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The debate took place in Burlington, North Carolina. You presented yourself as a 'common-sense' politician, downplaying some of the more progressive positions you had taken during the primaries. Bush struggled to get a handle on the situation, and the general consensus was that you came out on top.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1898, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 7725, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your response might have been a bit too aggressive and hostile. As a result, it's looking like more people are believing the allegations, even though some of your supporters are preaching your 'right-wing conspiracy' narrative.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1898, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 7726, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Millions of Americans watched the 60 Minutes interview; though perhaps many will continue to believe the allegations, many more are assured in your spouse’s, and your own sincere demeanor and responses. It is 1988, after all, right?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1899, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4421, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Well, that backfired. George Bush is out there touring the country, using the press to paint you as a pitiful loser for dodging the debate. Meanwhile, you're stuck ranting about the dishonest media, and corrupt GOP. Nice move, sir!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1900, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4422, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"In the best-case scenario, this complicates your attempt to win moderate voters. But you don't help matters by doubling down on this.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1901, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4424, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is probably the best you can do with this attack.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1902, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4426, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This seems to be an appeal towards working-class Americans on the question of education, slightly diverting the usual appeal to parents, and families, that is usually associated with education reform.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1902, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4425, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This seems to be an appeal to the poor, and minority communities of the country necessarily blocs to win, of course, in order for you to seize the Presidency.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1903, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4427, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is perfectly in line with your previous statements, particularly from the 1984 campaign, and, of course, your primary campaign this year; connecting the issues of foreign policy, and geopolitics to the American education system.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1904, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4428, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a good opening to remind voters of Bush's unpopularity and possible lack of judgment.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1904, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4429, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"If you want to take it a little bit easy, and avoid rehashing the Iran-Contra scandal this is probably the best move. A lot of advisors though, are upset that you are not taking a more aggressive line against the Vice President. Especially on this issue.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1905, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4430, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"You are definitely leaving a good attack on the table by bypassing this.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1906, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4431, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The Democratic base is happy, but this definitely puts you on the liberal end of the debate.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1906, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4432, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is probably the best hedge you could take on this ‘hot potato’ issue.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1907, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4433, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Core supporters are frustrated by this position.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1908, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4434, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"While this is, of course, true, this is not sound rhetoric if your trying to win the moderate, let alone the conservative voter in 1988.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1909, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4435, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This might be the best way to deal with this attack. Getting in the weeds about specifics might backfire or, more likely, create ammunition for the Atwater machine to utilize against you.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1910, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4436, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is an interesting response. It is a bit of a flip-flop, but regardless you are fighting the notion of yourself being a dove or weak on defense.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1911, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4437, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"While, yes. This is most in line with your actual positions, and the views of many Atari Democrats on the military budget, the Bush campaign is eager to spin this sentiment into associating you with the dovishness, and peace movements of the 1960s, and 1970s.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1912, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4438, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Despite your attempt to sugar-coat it, this is still considered a slightly dovish answer and will continue to fuel right-wing attacks. That said, it’s not that far from the mainstream.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1913, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4439, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is certainly a hawkish answer, though some good might come of it; by appealing to moderates and conservatives, it is sure to alienate young and liberal voters, though.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1914, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4440, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This sort of language certainly alienates some conservative Democrats and is something of a flip-flop. At the same time, it could help turn out labor and liberal voters.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1915, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4441, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Some fellow Democrats and liberals are still upset at your refusal to use the L-word. But at the same time, it was expected; it has been your strategy since 1984, hoping to ‘convert’ moderates and even some conservatives back to the Democratic Party.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1916, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4442, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This seems like a waffle to many voters, and doesn't convey the strength that is expected from a President.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1917, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4444, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This still doesn’t do much to improve your standing with labor, but your plan for infrastructure, which you touched upon quite heavily in both primary runs, is probably a smart move..\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1918, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4445, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Fair enough. Some of the more liberal voters within the Democratic Party are still unhappy, but they’ll vote for you anyway, right?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1918, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4443, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your tepid and vague tone wasn’t lost on the news media and those within the party. The Democratic Party isn’t by any means falling apart, but you still do have a problem with some elements of the party.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1919, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4446, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your advertisements are running well, but the Bush campaign, or more accurately, organizations 'supporting the Bush campaign', are hitting you on the 'integrity question' and your 'McGovern-ite' record, and you have no counter punch.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1921, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 445151, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is about the best you can do at this point, sir. The party establishment is seriously disturbed by your rhetoric, and despite your efforts to patch things up, more and more Governors and Congressmen are throwing their support behind Paul Tsongas's bid.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1921, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 444949, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This comes from the classic, tried-and-true Washington playbook for handling third-party candidates: just ignore them. But, sir, at this point, it looks like you've permanently severed ties with parts of the party, and more and more Congressmen and Governors are throwing their support behind Tsongas. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1920, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4447, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"These ads are certainly aggressive and do something to motivate the base, but where is your platform? Where are your beliefs?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1920, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4447, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The economy might prove to be your biggest opening throughout the election. Though there isn’t by any means an active recession, there is economic anxiety and a growing disillusionment with Reaganomics.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1921, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44491, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This comes from the classic, tried-and-true Washington playbook for handling third-party candidates: just ignore them. But while not every part of the Democratic Party is fully behind you, focusing too much on those dissenting voices could be a big mistake. It’s probably better to stick to what’s working. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1921, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4449, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This comes from the classic, tried-and-true Washington playbook for handling third-party candidates: just ignore them. But while not every part of the Democratic Party is fully behind you, focusing too much on those dissenting voices could be a big mistake. It’s probably better to stick to what’s working. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1921, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4448, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"While it’s true that the popularity of Ronald Reagan himself, and his economic agenda is fading slightly, some advisors think your ads were ‘boring’ compared to the attack ads being released by the Atwater Machine.’\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1922, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4450, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your own biography always plays well.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1923, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4451, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"John Anderson might not be polling as a serious contender, but your instincts are right, if you’re not smart about this, he could siphon off just enough voters to hurt us. We need to be strategic here.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1923, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44511, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"As of right now, it looks unlikely that McCloskey will even be on the ballot in many states, for a proactive strategy never hurt anyone, right?\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1924, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4452, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"It never hurts to remind the voters of your time in the military.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1925, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4453, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"It never hurts to remind the voters of your time in the military.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1926, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4454, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"It doesn't matter so much how to stack up to Bush -- anything you can do to subliminally convey that you <em>get</em> military matters is helpful.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1928, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4458, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This aligns perfectly with your statements on economics and inequality during the primaries, but some in your camp are confused, expecting you to shift to the right, or move away from a 'poverty message,' now that the real battle has begun. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1929, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4459, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a bold and personal take, and with television news airing your remarks almost every night, the Bush campaign and his family are furious. Turning this race into a street fight might be the right strategy, though it will be obviously divisive. \"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1933, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 44613, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The fact that your speech was more liberal than expected, was not missed by the pundits, and even some in the audience. Though, the party is a bit divided, this was also your opportunity to properly introduce yourself to the rest of the country, apart from Democrats, and for better or worse, you came across as: liberal.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1934, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4465, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Many in the press noted Senator Glenn’s reluctance to ‘get into the trench’ with Dan Quayle, despite the widespread belief that the debate would be raucous. The debate ended up being unnoteworthy, and tame. For that reason alone, it is considered a victory for the Bush campaign.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1934, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 3365, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is what many in the press wanted. A raucous, loose, and aggressive debate, filled with zingers and one-liners. At the end of the night, Senator Glenn was the winner, backing Senator Quayle in a corner, during nearly every question. Conservatives, though, are uniform in their belief that Glenn and Democrats alike are too aggressive.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1944, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4478, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"As capital punishment becomes an issue, it's difficult to find a position that doesn't alienate some group of your potential voters, and this is no different. Many base supporters, and espically minority voters, and activists are upset with your position.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1945, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4479, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"As capital punishment becomes an issue, it's difficult to find a position that doesn't alienate some group of your potential voters.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1947, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4480, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Unfortunately, this position alienates you with moderates in the current high-crime environment, and is nothing short of an enormous opening for the Bush campaign.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1948, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4481, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Don’t cheat, Jeb.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1949, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4481, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your statement is well-received by some, especially middle-class folks. But still, proposing tax cuts during the current deficit and debt hurts the ‘fiscally sane’ image that moderate Democrats, including yourself, have been trying to project.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1950, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4482, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"This statement brings cheers from all corners of the party.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1951, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4483, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your candor is noted by the press, and appreciated by your base. Republicans are without a doubt trying to twist, and use this statement as evidence towards your ‘Tax Hike Agenda’, but it doesn’t seem to be sticking…\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1953, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4484, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"After Mondale’s famous comments at the 1984 convention, this sort of statement does nothing but give the Republican ad machine more ammunition to portray you as a ‘Tax and Spend Liberal’, especially with your ‘have to be raised’ statement.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1958, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4490, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Considering your campaign and message on trade so far, this is a slight tack toward the left, but it could be vital in turning out the key labor vote, particularly in the Midwest.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1959, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4489, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This was the expected answer from you. Of course, labor and liberals are unhappy with this position, but many moderate voters hold warm feelings toward your campaign.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1960, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4491, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This answer shocked some supporters and many in the press who, since the 1984 campaign, have known you to be an advocate of free trade and centrism. Though labor is obviously jubilant, this is a big flip-flop and alienates voters.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1974, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4501, \"candidate\": 155, \"answer_feedback\": \"Blank man, sir guy, sir man, sir guy..\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1975, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4503, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Don’t cheat, Jeb.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1976, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4503, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is certainly the best way you could come out in favor of gun control leglsiation, but that said, this does sting with conservative, and rural Americans.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1982, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4511, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"This appears too much of a pander to Texans to go over well, when it runs against the normal principles of your party.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1983, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4511, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is a bold position, but it could definitely help some Texans make up their minds.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1983, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4512, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is obviously a ‘business-minded’ approach, but it might be a good appeal to those in oil-producing states, and generally to moderates, and even conservatives. Though it might bother environmentalists.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1984, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4513, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Some environmentalist-influenced supporters disagree, and this is considered something a flubbed answer from you. Many think you had an opportunity to reach out to Texas Democrats.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1985, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4514, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is not the preferred answer for this situation. The Bush campaign is eager to push the image of your campaign being ‘activist’ and ‘liberal’, for this position, notably lining your words up to a George McGovern speech in a nationally aired T.V advertisement.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1986, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4515, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is not a popular answer in the farm states and surprisingly glib, and callous on economic plight for a Democrat; many farmers and some workers in the Midwest find themselves more aligned with the Republican Party, on the basis of this statement alone.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1987, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4515, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is not a popular answer in the farm states and surprisingly glib, and callous on economic plight for a Democrat; many farmers and some workers in the Midwest find themselves more aligned with the Republican Party, on the basis of this statement alone.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1988, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4517, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"You seem to be admitting that the Reagan Administration made a big mistake here, and that you either contributed or were not involved in the big choices.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1989, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4517, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is certainly considered a move toward the left, considering much of your past centrist rhetoric on federal intervention. But with the gravity of the farm crisis, this might be a wise strategy, at the cost of alienating some moderate and conservative voters.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1989, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9999, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your focus on the Midwest might be a good choice, as the Bush campaign has been making ground there in some recent polls. Your speech goes over well, though some liberals and now Republicans are saying: ‘Where’s The Beef?’\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1989, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9998, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Since the 1984 campaign, it’s become clear to the national press that your relationship with the African American community is practically non-existent. As such, making inroads, and stressing your commitment to every part of the coalition is necessary.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1989, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 9997, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"While you are making ground in states like Montana, Idaho, and the Dakotas, the Bush campaign is taking advantage of this little detour, and pushing hard into the Midwest, with ads and rallies.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1989, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4516, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This certainly hurts your standing with farmers, who have been trending more Democratic during this crisis. At the same time, this sentiment resonates with some moderate and conservative voters.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1990, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4518, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1991, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4518, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1992, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4519, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1993, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4519, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1994, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4520, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1995, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4520, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1996, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4521, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1997, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4521, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Good luck tomorrow!\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1998, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4523, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Dukakis attacks you relentlessly for refusing to debate, and it is not helping your position.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 1999, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4523, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your campaign has always carried a raw, somewhat unconventional patriotism for a Democrat. But that messaging might be exactly what works against George Bush in the general election, and relying on it could be a smart move.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 2000, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4524, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Unfortunately, Dukakis performed pretty well in these debates, and you seemed to miss a beat on a couple occassions.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 2001, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4524, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"The country does have a trade deficit with Japan and other nations, and you’ve been talking about this for years, long before your presidential run. That said, the issue has much less resonance outside of the Midwest, and might not be the best national message to run on.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 2003, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4525, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is similar to the kind of personal attacks you used during the primaries. George Bush might be especially vulnerable to this, with the 'wimp' image still hanging over him in the public’s mind. However, if you push too far, you risk coming off as erratic, maybe even cruel.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 2004, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4526, \"candidate\": 152, \"answer_feedback\": \"Your debates with Dukakis were largely inconclusive, and analysts agree that they are unlikely to affect the race.\"}}, {\"model\": \"campaign_trail.answer_feedback\", \"pk\": 2005, \"fields\": {\"answer\": 4526, \"candidate\": 153, \"answer_feedback\": \"This is the same messaging that arguably won you the Democratic nomination. That said, some on your staff still believe that, regardless of its success, you should’ve refined your approach.\"}}]");
